 "strategy": {
  "summary": "Buy a sharp dip and sell when the price snaps back. Each bar the strategy measures how far the close sits below its moving average, in units of recent volatility (a z-score). When that z-score falls to the entry level it buys at the next bar's open, and it sells once the z-score recovers to the exit level, after a maximum number of bars, or at an optional stop.",
  "formula": "z = (close \u2212 average of the last N closes) \u00f7 standard deviation of the last M closes",
  "rules": [
   {
    "label": "Buy",
    "text": "When z closes at or below the entry level (\u22121.5 to \u22123). With confirmation on, the signal bar must also close above the previous bar's close. The order fills at the next bar's open."
   },
   {
    "label": "Sell",
    "text": "At the next open after z closes at or above the exit level, or once the position has been held the max number of bars. An optional stop sits k \u00d7 ATR(14) below the entry and fills the moment it is touched."
   },
   {
    "label": "Size",
    "text": "Long only, one position at a time. As many whole ES contracts as the account covers at full contract value (no leverage), starting from $1,000,000."
   }
  ],
